From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: refuse a banned non-AP MLD by its MLD address

The ubus ban check in hostapd_ubus_handle_event() compares the source
address of the frame. A non-AP MLD sends its Authentication frames from
a link address, and its Basic Multi-Link element names its MLD address.
A ban of the MLD address thus misses the Authentication frame. It also
misses a (Re)Association Request that hostapd matches to the station by
the MLD address of the Multi-Link element (handle_mlo_translate()),
where the driver did not translate the addresses.

Give the request the MLD address of a non-AP MLD. handle_auth() takes it
from the Multi-Link element, as its ACL check does; handle_assoc() takes
it from the station entry. The ban check tests the MLD address first and
the link address after it, so a ban of a link address still refuses it.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -4395,6 +4395,7 @@ static void handle_auth(struct hostapd_d
 		.type = HOSTAPD_UBUS_AUTH_REQ,
 		.mgmt_frame = mgmt,
 		.ssi_signal = rssi,
+		.mld_addr = mld_sta ? sa : NULL,
 	};
 
 	auth_alg = le_to_host16(mgmt->u.auth.auth_alg);
@@ -7877,6 +7878,7 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 		.type = HOSTAPD_UBUS_ASSOC_REQ,
 		.mgmt_frame = mgmt,
 		.ssi_signal = rssi,
+		.mld_addr = ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) ? sta->addr : NULL,
 	};
 
 	/* followed by SSID and Supported rates; and HT capabilities if 802.11n
